<given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Luo</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Shiojima</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Bialik</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Fulton</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Lefer</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Sessa</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Walsh</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The HMG-CoA reductase inhibitor simvastatin activates the protein kinase Akt and promotes angiogenesis in normocholesterolemic animals</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>6</volume><issue>9</issue><fpage>1004</fpage><lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10973320</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/79510</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kojro</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Gimpl</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Lammich</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Marz</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahrenholz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Low cholesterol stimulates the nonamyloidogenic pathway by its effect on the alpha -secretase ADAM 10</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci USA</source><year>2001</year><volume>98</volume><issue>10</issue><fpage>5815</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11309494</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.081612998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shishehbor </surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Brennan</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Aviles</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></nam